@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# 0.6.0 boiling residual spike
+
+date: 2026-10-21
+plan: 0.6.0-plan.md (t15)
+evidence:
+	experiments/logs/2026-10-21-05_47-GPU-browser-tests.log
+	experiments/logs/2026-10-21-05_55-GPU-browser-tests.log
+	experiments/logs/2026-10-21-07_19-GPU-browser-tests.log
+	experiments/logs/2026-10-21-residual-spike.log
+
+## review
+
+t14 asked for a device capture that named the frame of the cycle residual spike.
+It arrived: fixed ns=4, dt=1/240, N=512, K20, two cycles, frame 301,
+absRes=49995, rhs=1915, true=26.11. The same run ends at true=0.0097. The
+auto-policy capture from the same machine does not spike (peaks 0.18-0.39, all
+at frame 1). Across the earlier fixed rows the peak grows with solver work:
+K60 68, K40 49, K20 26, 1-cycle 15, while the settled residual orders the other
+way (0.0079 / 0.0083 / 0.0097 / 0.013). A failed solve cannot do that.
+
+## what the spike is
+
+The reported residual was `b - L p` with `b` and `p` from the projection and
+`L` from mass and flags after transport and phase. A face weight that changes
+between those two moments, times a hydrostatic pressure jump, is the whole
+number. rhoVac=0.001 makes an emptied neighbor a weight of ~500.
+
+CPU proof (`experiments/residual-spike.js`):
+
+- drop one cell of a linear field to rhoVac: residual x499 (1.0e3 -> 5.0e5)
+- melt a blocked cell inside a uniform p=5e4: residual 0 -> 2.0e5
+- dam N=64, step 10: end/solve=556, solve/rhs=1.4e-4
+- dam N=128, 600 steps: max drift/solve=767, drift/rhs=0.36 at step 276,
+  solve/rhs stays 0.073
+- cycle N=128, 1400 steps: no spike through 2.5 s, then at step 1170
+  (t=4.875 s) the post-step residual is 1.2e4 times the solve and 668 times
+  the solve rhs. The hardware spike is the same scenario at the same sim time
+  (frame 301 is t=5.0 s, 1204 substeps). Its 26 is post-step residual over the
+  post-step rhs, sampled every 30 frames at N=512, so it is a sample of this
+  event rather than the same quotient. Jet at N=128 over 2.5 s does not spike.
+
+More K makes a larger pressure, so a larger drift. That is why the spike
+anti-correlates with the solve. The auto policy uses a smaller dt, moves less
+mass per step, and does not spike. No solver change follows from the spike.
+
+## changes
+
+- GPU: on a stats frame, the last substep reduces the residual after the
+  projection and before transport into stats slots 32/33. The existing stats
+  pass still evaluates the post-step operator and now writes that to slots
+  34/35. The two reductions do not share a bind group (`layout: "auto"`).
+- CPU: `project()` stores `diag.poissonRes/poissonRhs`. `stats()` reports that
+  as the solve and recomputes the post-step value as `poissonDrift`. The printed
+  drift ratio uses the post-step rhs, so it is the number the older logs called
+  `true`. A freeze can inflate it; health reads `true`, not `drift`.
+- Report, HUD snapshot and the log table print `drift` next to `true`. The
+  capture header says which is which.
+- Defaults unchanged. Third level stays rejected.
+
+## validation
+
+- `node experiments/residual-spike.js` passes (synthetic + dam N=64 wiring:
+  stored residual matches the pre-transport recompute).
+- `node experiments/run-all.js --quick`: 12/12.
+- `node experiments/gpu-mock.js`: the reduce is absent when stats are off, and
+  on a stats frame it runs once, after the last `applyGrad` and before
+  `advectMass`. WGSL brace/slot check passes.
+- Device confirmation: `experiments/logs/2026-10-21-07_19-GPU-browser-tests.log`,
+  same preset as `05_47` (cycle, N=512, ns=4, K20, 600 frames, Ampere).
+
+## device confirmation
+
+The split reads the pre-transport fields. Against `05_47`, which is the same
+trajectory to the printed digits (mass, phases, p[0..125940.546875], maxDiv):
+
+- frame 301 moved intact: drift=26.11078936008509, driftRes=49994.73828125,
+  the old absRes. 49994.73828125 / 26.11078936008509 = 1914.7157, the old rhs.
+- end of run: old `true` 0.009715138446710316 is the new `drift`. The solve is
+  res=16.50, rhs=1882.04, true=0.00877.
+- sampled true peak is 0.141 at frame 1 (cold start), not the boil.
+- press 1.193 vs 1.162 ms and stats 0.303 vs 0.275 ms. The extra reduce sits in
+  the press group on sampled frames. fps 104.2 vs 107.5 is run variance; the
+  reduce is not a frame-time change.
+
+## next
+
+The re-trial is in `archive/0.6.0-cycle-gate-worklog.md`. One cycle is rejected
+for dam, blobs, and cycle. Jet ships 1 cycle after the 08_02 pair. The open
+fps check is `python3 run_gpu_capture.py jet-auto`. Mac-cormack (t5) does not
+wait on that.
